# The Gradle wrapper is deliberately NOT ignored. Flutter's template excludes it,
# which means a fresh clone or a CI runner gets gradle-wrapper.properties — and
# so learns it wants Gradle 9.3.1 — but not the jar or the scripts needed to
# fetch it, and silently falls back to whatever Gradle happens to be installed.
# That produces "Unsupported class file major version" or an outright failure on
# a machine that has none, and the cause is not obvious from the error. Gradle's
# own recommendation is to commit all four files together.
/.gradle
/captures/
/local.properties
GeneratedPluginRegistrant.java
.cxx/
.kotlin/

# Remember to never publicly share your keystore.
# See https://flutter.dev/to/reference-keystore
key.properties
**/*.keystore
**/*.jks
